            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane H Bock"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was perfect for my brunch. I halved the apricot nectar, doubled the lemon juice and added a little extra (fresh)orange juice. I am going to use the leftover for smoothies as soon as I can buy fresh blueberries or mangos.",
            "datePublished": "2016-10-23T23:35:00.087Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NMChef1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this several times, exactly as written. (I guess Jumex had shrunk their cans of Apricot Nectar down from 12 ounces to 11.3, but since I had multiple cans, and I was already measuring out the 1-1/2 cups of orange juice, I also measured out 12 ounces of nectar.) I liked it, but I guess my palate wasn't discriminating enough to appreciate the combination of juices. It just wasn't anything special, to me.",
            "datePublished": "2013-11-03T14:51:56.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
